  "observations": [
    "tests/common/mod.rs at this commit still stores status.code().unwrap_or(1) at lines 375 and 394. fifo_opens_do_not_wait_for_a_peer asserts outcome.signal.is_none() at line 1739 before it accepts the exit. The independent oracle requires signal none and code Some(expected). killed_child_is_pass is false. This is not a required product fix for the FIFO closure.",
    "tls_wrong_host and tls_wrong_ca report stderr_exact true because expect_stderr was None. The scorer did not compare those bytes to a pre-registered string. The retained stderr is the static line error: transport transport connect failed, retryable false, not_replayed, and the same policy line. One TCP accept and zero HTTP completions is a failed handshake, recorded apart from the FIFO accept count of 0.",
    "process_owner still uses O_NOFOLLOW and create_new, without O_NONBLOCK, and only after inspect has accepted a regular token file.",
    "Linux ignores O_NONBLOCK on regular-file reads. Mode 0600 token and SQL queries, token 4096, token 4096 plus a newline, SQL 65536, a hard link, and a valid CA all exited 0.",
    "Device-node open bounds remain documented and unsigned.",
    "No failed probe attempt exists. attempt-1 is the only oracle run."
  ],
